  "title": "Kenesary Kasymov",
  "summary": "Kenesary Kasymov (1802–1847), grandson of Ablai Khan, led the largest 19th-century Kazakh uprising, begun in 1837 against Russian expansion and rule. Proclaimed khan in 1841, he was killed in 1847 after capture by Kirghiz fighters. Kazakhstan now treats him as a national hero.",
